<title>HONG KONG: HK's Wing Lee debuts at HK$2.10/share.</title>
<headline>HK's Wing Lee debuts at HK$2.10/share.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of electronic components manufacturer Wing Lee Holdings Ltd made their trading debut at HK$2.10 per share, compared with their issue price of HK$1.00 each.  </p>
<p>Wing Lee is a manufacturer of DC switches, jacks, AC sockets and speaker terminals.</p>
<p>It issued 70 million new shares at HK$1.00 each in its initial public offering of shares in Hong Kong, of which the 63 million shares offered to the public was 312.9 times subscribed.</p>
<p>Wing Lee said it would use the net proceeds of about HK$59.5 million to expand and upgrade production facilities and machineries in Hong Kong and China, and for repayment of bank loans and for working capital.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
